WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.615
This is your first more independent table-writing
exercise Do not

00:00:05.628 --> 00:00:10.604
start from a blank screen mentally Use the comments
and earlier examples

00:00:10.631 --> 00:00:16.135
as a pattern Decide what one row in your small table
represents

00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:20.993
Choose a primary key identify which columns are
required and add a

00:00:21.006 --> 00:00:25.993
simple CHECK or other rule where it makes sense Then
insert one

00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:31.076
valid row and run a SELECT to inspect it Use the
browser

00:00:31.102 --> 00:00:36.832
editor and run your code in small steps if needed If
PostgreSQL

00:00:36.858 --> 00:00:40.108
reports an error read it carefully and fix one issue
at a

00:00:40.135 --> 00:00:45.704
time The slide includes one possible answer but try
your own version

00:00:45.731 --> 00:00:51.010
first The purpose is to practice translating a small
design into executable

00:00:51.023 --> 00:00:54.220
PostgreSQL not to reproduce one exact script
